4.integrations\u002Findex",{"title":479,"path":480,"stem":481},"Lovable payments with Vatly","\u002Fintegrations\u002Flovable","4.integrations\u002F1.lovable",{"title":483,"path":484,"stem":485},"Bolt payments with Vatly","\u002Fintegrations\u002Fbolt","4.integrations\u002F2.bolt",{"id":487,"title":488,"body":489,"description":721,"extension":722,"links":723,"meta":724,"navigation":725,"path":175,"seo":726,"stem":176,"__hash__":727},"docs\u002F3.packages\u002F10.fluentcart\u002F01.merchant-of-record.md","Merchant-of-Record invoicing: implementation notes",{"type":490,"value":491,"toc":714},"minimark",[492,504,509,521,532,536,561,572,647,651,698,709],[493,494,495,496,503],"p",{},"How the plugin makes Vatly the single source of truth for invoices on FluentCart\norders, and the FluentCart integration points it relies on. This is reference\nmaterial for maintainers; end users only need the ",[497,498,502],"a",{"href":499,"rel":500},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fvatly\u002Fvatly-fluentcart-wp\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002FREADME.md",[501],"nofollow","README",".",[505,506,508],"h2",{"id":507},"the-problem","The problem",[493,510,511,512,516,517,520],{},"Vatly is the Merchant of Record, so the legally valid VAT invoice (and, for\nrefunds, the credit note) is the one ",[513,514,515],"strong",{},"Vatly"," issues. FluentCart also generates\nits own receipt\u002Finvoice. Left alone, a customer paying via Vatly would receive\n",[513,518,519],{},"two competing invoices"," for one purchase.",[493,522,523,524,528,529,503],{},"The plugin therefore (a) surfaces Vatly's invoice and (b) suppresses\nFluentCart's own invoicing, but only for orders paid via the Vatly gateway\n(",[525,526,527],"code",{},"payment_method === 'vatly'","). Every guard callback is a strict no-op for\nnon-Vatly orders. The guard lives in ",[525,530,531],{},"src\u002FSupport\u002FMoRInvoiceGuard.php",[505,533,535],{"id":534},"hooks-used","Hooks used",[537,538,539],"blockquote",{},[493,540,541,544,545,548,549,552,553,556,557,560],{},[513,542,543],{},"FluentCart version note."," The gateway integration (registration, checkout,\nrefunds, and the ",[525,546,547],{},"order.paid"," confirmation + Vatly-invoice stamping) has been\nported to and verified against ",[513,550,551],{},"FluentCart free 2.2.0",". The two\nMerchant-of-Record email\u002Freceipt guard hooks in the table below still carry\ntheir original ",[525,554,555],{},"\u002F\u002F verified: FluentCart free 1.3.28"," file:line references and\nhave ",[513,558,559],{},"not"," yet been re-verified against 2.2.0: the hook names and line\nnumbers may have moved, so re-confirm they still exist and fire before relying\non the email-suppression guard on 2.2.0.",[493,562,563,564,567,568,571],{},"The guard wires only hooks confirmed to exist ",[513,565,566],{},"and fire",". Each wired hook\ncarries a ",[525,569,570],{},"\u002F\u002F verified: …"," file:line comment in the source.",[573,574,575,591],"table",{},[576,577,578],"thead",{},[579,580,581,585,588],"tr",{},[582,583,584],"th",{},"Intent",[582,586,587],{},"FluentCart hook",[582,589,590],{},"Notes",[592,593,594,630],"tbody",{},[579,595,596,600,610],{},[597,598,599],"td",{},"Suppress FluentCart's competing customer receipt\u002Finvoice email (and its PDF attachment)",[597,601,602,605,606,609],{},[525,603,604],{},"fluent_cart\u002Fshould_send_email_notification"," (filter, ",[525,607,608],{},"EmailNotificationMailer::mailEmailsOfEvent",")",[597,611,612,613,616,617,620,621,624,625,629],{},"Returns ",[525,614,615],{},"false"," for the ",[525,618,619],{},"order_paid_customer"," notification (event ",[525,622,623],{},"order_paid",", subject \"Purchase Receipt #",[626,627],"binding",{"value":628},"order.invoice_no","\") on Vatly orders: the only customer mail that doubles as FluentCart's invoice and the only one that can attach FluentCart's PDF receipt. No email ⇒ no competing invoice and no attached PDF (covers Pro too). All other notifications (refunds, shipping, subscription, and every admin copy) pass through untouched.",[579,631,632,635,644],{},[597,633,634],{},"Surface the Vatly invoice link on the customer receipt page",[597,636,637,640,641,609],{},[525,638,639],{},"fluent_cart\u002Freceipt\u002Fthank_you\u002Fafter_order_items"," (action, ",[525,642,643],{},"ThankYouRender",[597,645,646],{},"Auto-renders the Vatly invoice button (reusing the shortcode renderer) beneath the order items for Vatly orders.",[505,648,650],{"id":649},"why-some-surfaces-arent-hooked","Why some surfaces aren't hooked",[652,653,654,678,684],"ul",{},[655,656,657,660,661,664,665,668,669,672,673,677],"li",{},[513,658,659],{},"FluentCart Pro PDF receipt"," (",[525,662,663],{},"fluent_cart\u002Fpdf\u002Fgenerate_receipt",") only fires\nunder Pro + FluentPDF (",[525,666,667],{},"OrderService::canGenerateReceiptPdf()"," +\n",[525,670,671],{},"defined('FLUENT_PDF')","), so it never runs on free. Suppressing the receipt\n",[674,675,676],"em",{},"email"," already drops its PDF attachment on Pro, so no separate handler is\nneeded.",[655,679,680,683],{},[513,681,682],{},"Refund PDF \u002F refund URL",": FluentCart free exposes no hook to redirect a\nrefund PDF, and there is no free refund-PDF surface to gate.",[655,685,686,689,690,693,694,697],{},[513,687,688],{},"Admin billing-detail edits",": FluentCart free fires no action or filter\naround ",[525,691,692],{},"CustomerAddressResource::update"," or the admin\n",[525,695,696],{},"CustomerController::updateAddress",", so an admin edit of an order's\u002Fcustomer's\nbilling address cannot be blocked or mirrored.",[493,699,700,701,704,705,708],{},"These FluentCart-side artifacts remain FluentCart-local and ",[513,702,703],{},"non-authoritative",";\nVatly's invoice and credit note are the legal record of account. For\nsubscriptions, point staff to the Vatly customer portal\n(",[525,706,707],{},"SubscriptionService::updateBillingUrl()",") when billing details must change; a\nFluentCart-local edit never reaches Vatly's already-issued invoice.",[537,710,711],{},[493,712,713],{},"Earlier revisions referenced several FluentCart hook names that don't exist in\ncore; those have been removed. If you extend the guard, confirm any new hook\nactually fires in the FluentCart version you target before relying on it.",{"title":715,"searchDepth":716,"depth":716,"links":717},"",2,[718,719,720],{"id":507,"depth":716,"text":508},{"id":534,"depth":716,"text":535},{"id":649,"depth":716,"text":650},"How the plugin makes Vatly the single source of truth for invoices on FluentCart orders, and the FluentCart integration points it relies on.","md",null,{},{"title":174},{"title":488,"description":721},"LwbqdKGrcXNEQxeKK_AviU2IcEG96_DGkpWVL1kXE4Y",[729,731],{"title":129,"path":171,"stem":172,"description":730,"children":-1},"Accept payments through Vatly in FluentCart, the WordPress e-commerce plugin.",{"title":129,"path":183,"stem":184,"description":732,"children":-1},"Sell Paid Memberships Pro (PMPro) memberships through Vatly.",1795611371092]